// An index that changes the text it looks into, where the value is only looked at (`print`, an
// operand, a receiver): the text is what the index looks into, so it may not be changed by a later
// part (choice 1382). Compiled code read the old text after the change had freed it.
nint cut(ref string text) {
    text = "a new text that takes another block of memory".clone()
    return 2
}

void main() {
    var s = "abc, an old text long enough to be on the heap".clone()
    print(s[cut(ref s)])
}
